<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102768" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέγος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέγος</span>
			, <i>roof</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.333
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.559
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.64
			</span></i>, al. (never in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1126
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1488
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Sam.</u>
				246
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				3.40
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὑπὶ τοῦ τέγους</span> you on
			the <i>roof!</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1502
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>V.</u>
				68
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶ μ᾽ ἀπὸ τοῦ τέγους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					262
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				3.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τοῦ οἰκήματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.48
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				7.5.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HG</u>
				4.4.12
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> any
				<i>covered hall</i> or <i>chamber</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. Παρνάσιον</span> the temple at Delphi, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				5.41
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιθίνῳ ἔνδον τέγει</span>,
			i.e. in a cave, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>N.</u>
				3.54
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> later,
				<i>brothel, stew,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				11.363
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				12.13.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				6.143
			</span></i>. (Not found in Trag.) (Cf. Lat. <i>tego.</i>)</div>
